    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2UyR1EqUZEYkn7v6jWwzw5D)_\n\n## What\n- New module `sp-collection-query-tables-book` (the `sp-collection-query-tables` family already exists, so this is a new part of it, not a new family): a table of the sections of a note tagged `book` or `collection`, sorted by page.\n  - Sections are notes whose `bib-parent` links to the book. It is an ordinary query spec (`:parent-of` + `:parent-prop \"bib-parent\"` + `:sort-by :page`), so every renderer, saved views and dynamic blocks work with it.\n  - `C-c w b` / `M-x sp-collec-query-book-open` opens it for the note at point (the book, or one of its sections); elsewhere it asks for a book.\n- Two new columns in the core: `:pages` (text of `pub-pages`) and `:page` (its first number, used for sorting). Sections with no number (e.g. roman numerals) sort last.\n- New `vulpea-ui` widget \"Book position\" (`sp-collection-query-tables-book-widget`, order 345): the book as a button, \"Section N of M\", previous/next buttons, and all sections in page order with the current one marked. It uses the same data function as the table (`sp-collec-query-book-position`). Registered like the Link inbox widgets, and loaded after `vulpea-ui`.\n- Literate doc `sp-collection-query-tables.org` updated in bullets; the `.el` files tangled from it.\n\n## Page property: `pub-pages`\nI used the existing `pub-pages` meta key. The schemas in `sp-vulpea-schemas` already define it for `booksection`, `incollection` and `journalarticle`, so no new key is needed. Its value is text (`12-34`, `pp. 12-34`) and the table sorts on the first number in it. Say so if you would rather have a separate numeric key.\n\n## Tested\n- 6 ERT tests in Emacs 29.3 batch (`tests/sp-collection-query-tables-book-test.el`) with Vulpea stubbed: first-page parsing, the new columns, page order, root detection, position/previous/next, the spec.\n- **Not run:** the widget (needs `vui`/`vulpea-ui` and a sidebar), the table renderers, or anything against the real vault. The widget's layout and its order relative to the other widgets are worth a look: open a chapter litnote, `C-x t s`.\n\nNo CHANGELOG edit, per the nightly-tidy rule.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiBucimHCJ8fQCvMaMF)_",
